 href="/encyclopedia/ingauni"><span class="enc-name">Ingauni</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ingauni were a Ligurian people of the western Riviera of Italy, centred on Albium Ingaunum, modern Albenga.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/inge-sargent"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/inge-sargent.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Inge Sargent</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Inge Sargent is an Austrian-born writer who married Sao Kya Seng, the saopha of the Shan state of Hsipaw, whom she met as a student in the United States.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ingelger"><span class="enc-name">Ingelger</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ingelger was a 9th-century Frankish noble regarded as the founder of the first dynasty of the counts of Anjou.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ingelheim-am-rhein"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ingelheim-am-rhein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ingelheim am Rhein</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ingelheim am Rhein is a town in Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany, on the Rhine west of Mainz.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ingiloys"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ingiloys.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ingiloys</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ingiloys are a Georgian-speaking ethnographic group of north-western Azerbaijan, living mainly in the Qakh, Zaqatala and Balakan districts.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ingolstadt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ingolstadt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ingolstadt</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ingolstadt is a city in Upper Bavaria, Germany, on the Danube.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ingria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ingria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ingria</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ingria is a historical region on the southern shore of the Gulf of Finland, around present-day St Petersburg.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ingrian-finns"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ingrian-finns.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ingrian Finns</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ingrian Finns are the Lutheran Finnish-speaking population of Ingria, around the Gulf of Finland and modern St Petersburg.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ingrian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ingrian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ingrian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 1610–1617</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ingrian War was fought between Sweden and the Tsardom of Russia during and after Russia's Time of Troubles.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ingush-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ingush-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ingush people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ingush are a Nakh people of the central North Caucasus, closely related to the Chechens, living mainly in the Republic of Ingushetia in Russia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/thingvellir"><img class="enc-thumb" sr